      "writtenOn": "2026-03-12T22:51:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ok, so there will be padding after this member, right?\nI\u0027ve seen quite often an explicit padding being added in iocts, so in this case:\n```\nstruct zram_android_ioc_data {\n\t__u32 version;\n\t__u32 pad;\n...\n}\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 38,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 38,
        "endChar": 15
      },
      "revId": "f9a7d8c82300c9f36b80e9f17a954b6799032bb3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d36f3b62_6758fa36",
        "filename": "include/uapi/linux/zram_ioctl.h",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 47,
      "author": {
        "id": 1157738
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-03-12T22:51:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Since you just return a number, you could use the ioctl return value:\n\n```\n#define ZRAM_ANDROID_IOC_GET_VERSION\t_IO(ZRAM_ANDROID_IOC_MAGIC, 0)\n```\n\nAnd in zram_ioctl() just return the version number without any copy_to_user():\n\n```\nif (cmd \u003d\u003d ZRAM_ANDROID_IOC_GET_VERSION)\n\treturn ZRAM_ANDROID_IOC_VERSION;\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 46,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 47,
        "endChar": 39
      },
